  "reading": {
   "title": "Practice for the interview",
   "text": "Hafsa has a job interview at Lincoln Elementary School on Friday. She is nervous, so she practices at home with her son Emre.\n\nEmre plays the principal. \"Have you ever worked with children?\" he asks. Hafsa thinks for a moment. \"Yes, I have. I have volunteered in a school library for two years.\" Emre smiles. \"Good! Have you ever taught a class?\" \"No, I haven't,\" says Hafsa. \"I have never taught a class alone, but I have helped many teachers.\"\n\n\"Have you ever lived abroad?\" Emre asks. \"Yes, I have. I have lived in two countries, and I have visited three. I think that is a good experience for a teacher.\"\n\nEmre claps. \"Great answers! Have you ever felt this ready?\" Hafsa laughs. \"No, never!\"",
   "glossary": [
    {
     "en": "nervous",
     "tr": "gergin"
    },
    {
     "en": "for a moment",
     "tr": "bir an için"
    },
    {
     "en": "clap",
     "tr": "alkışlamak"
    },
    {
     "en": "ready",
     "tr": "hazır"
    }
   ],
